    "content": "Chuck Norris (born Carlos Ray Norris in 1940, died March 2026) was an American martial artist, actor, and producer, renowned as a six-time undefeated world karate champion and a leading 1980s action star. He is best known for his role in \"Walker, Texas Ranger\" (1993–2001) and for launching his acting career against Bruce Lee in \"The Way of the Dragon\" (1972). Martial Arts Career: Norris began training in South Korea while in the Air Force, later winning the World Professional Middleweight Karate Championship in 1968. He holds an eighth-degree black belt in Tae Kwon Do and founded his own style, Chun Kuk Do. Film & TV Star: He starred in films like Missing in Action, The Delta Force, and Code of Silence. Personal Life & Family: Born in Ryan, Oklahoma, on March 10, 1940, he was 86 at the time of his death. He was married to Dianne Holechek (two children, Mike and Eric) and later Gena O'Kelley (twins, Dakota and Danilee). Pop Culture Status: In his later years, he became an internet sensation, inspiring the humorous \"Chuck Norris Facts\" that highlighted his reputation for extreme strength. Note: Reports indicate Chuck Norris passed away on March 20, 2026, surrounded by his family, notes Instagram.",
